Original dual-ABI native imports for the opt-in Apple support boundary.

Interface facts: public LGPL Wine-derived host declarations identify nine NT
imports used with Microsoft x64 ABI by libd3dshared. Implementations here are
original adapters over upstream Wine 11 signatures/bodies; no CrossOver code
is imported. Existing internal SysV calls retain their implementations. The
only ABI selector is the return address inside the explicitly selected dylib's
executable __TEXT span obtained via public dladdr/getsegmentdata metadata.
No Apple code, imports, objects or private globals are modified.

Interface reference (declarations and calling-convention facts only):
https://github.com/Alien4042x/WineForge/blob/df3d347fd59ebe932affeb83c6a39fe34abf39e8/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
SHA-256: 9b811058545eb74fc933e994e8b4408cfef5fe11e95e8dcc1f42081b70c87036

Apply after d3dmetal-wine-11.0-non-native-regions.patch. Off by default.
This source is LGPL-2.1-or-later, matching Wine. Capability remains unaccepted
until both ABI argument tests and actual API/render/lifecycle tests pass.

